    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Bright, Beautifully Finished Owner occupied two-Bedroom Apartment in the Heart of East Wall, Dublin 3\r\n\r\nHORAN ESTATES are delighted to introduce Apartment 20, The Lighthouse — a spacious two-bedroom, two-bathroom apartment set on the second floor within this striking development, offering contemporary living with the added bonus of a private balcony boasting panoramic views across the Dublin skyline. Finished to a high standard throughout with warm timber-effect flooring, sleek white decor and modern fittings, this home is ready to move straight into.\r\n\r\n\r\nLocation\r\n\r\nChurch Road places residents in one of Dublin's most convenient and up-and-coming city-fringe neighbourhoods, East Wall. The area enjoys excellent connectivity to the City Centre, the Docklands, and the IFSC, all just a short walk or cycle away. Local amenities include a SPAR convenience store on-site, landscaped communal courtyards, and easy access to the 3Arena, East Point Business Park, and the Point Village. Excellent public transport links are on the doorstep, with Dublin Bus routes, the Luas Red Line, and Docklands/Connolly rail stations all within easy reach, making this an ideal base for  commuting into the city.\r\n\r\nHoran Estates recommend viewing this property to fully appreciate the quality of finish and the setting it has to offer.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, furniture, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs are provided for guidance only. Furniture shown is for representation purposes only; please consult the estate agent to confirm what will remain in the property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall (6.90 sq. m / 1.51m x 6.13m)\r\nA welcoming and surprisingly generous hallway connecting all principal rooms, with two additional closets (1.12 sq. m and 1.94 sq. m) providing excellent extra storage.\r\n\r\nLiving/Dining Room (15.12 sq. m / 4.05m x 4.16m)\r\nA bright, well-proportioned reception room with sliding door access to the private balcony, wall-mounted TV point, and plenty of space for both dining and lounging furniture.\r\n\r\nBalcony (5.42 sq. m / 3.99m x 1.36m)\r\nA generous private outdoor terrace running the width of the living room, enjoying elevated views across neighbouring rooftops and the Dublin skyline beyond.\r\n\r\nKitchen (4.65 sq. m / 2.54m x 1.83m)\r\nA sleek, separately fitted kitchen with contemporary handleless units, marble-effect splashback and worktops, integrated Whirlpool washing machine-dryer, dishwasher, oven, hob, and stainless-steel sink with chrome mixer tap.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (13.29 sq. m / 3.01m x 4.58m)\r\nA large double bedroom with fitted wardrobe storage, ceiling coat rail, and the benefit of a private en suite shower room.\r\n\r\nEn Suite Shower Room (3.28 sq. m / 1.79m x 1.83m)\r\nFully tiled in marble-effect finish, comprising curved glass shower enclosure with rainfall shower head, WC, and vanity unit wash-hand basin.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (12.64 sq. m / 2.90m x 4.60m)\r\nA second well-sized double bedroom, bright and neutrally decorated, with fitted wardrobe and ceiling coat rail.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom (4.58 sq. m / 2.54m x 1.81m)\r\nBeautifully finished in marble-effect tiling with an illuminated arched mirror, panelled bath with overhead shower, WC and vanity unit wash-hand basin.\r\n\r\nIn total, the apartment extends to approximately 65 sq. m (700 sq. ft) of well-planned living space."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "BER C1 – A well-insulated, energy-efficient home helping keep running costs down.\r\nSecure underground designated parking space and visitor parking too\r\nEn Suite Bathroom – The main bedroom benefits from its own private shower room.\r\nModern Fitted Kitchen – Sleek handleless units, marble-effect splashback, integrated Whirlpool washing machine-dryer, dishwasher and oven\r\nPrivate Balcony – 5.42 sq. m of outdoor space with sweeping views over Dublin's rooftops and skyline.\r\nTwo Generous Double Bedrooms – 13.29 sq. m and 12.64 sq. m, both with fitted wardrobe storage.\r\nExcellent Storage Throughout – Multiple built-in closets, including a dedicated hall storage room.\r\nBright Open-Plan Living/Dining Room – 15.12 sq. m, flooded with natural light and opening directly onto the balcony.\r\nHigh Floor Position – Elevated outlook over surrounding period rooftops and the city beyond.\r\nSuperb City-Fringe Location – Moments from the Docklands, IFSC and city centre, with excellent transport links on the doorstep."
      },
      {
